title: 'collator-discovery: keep a reserved peer whose address set changed'

doc:
  - audience: Node Operator
    description: |
      The collator-discovery reserved-peer refresh removed peers by multiaddr: when a selected
      peer republished its authority-discovery record with a different address set, every
      address that disappeared turned into a removal of that peer, while the addresses that
      stayed produced no addition, so the peer silently lost its reservation until its record
      changed again. A collator restart triggers exactly this, because the node publishes its
      record before it has discovered all of its external addresses. The refresh now removes
      only the peers that have no address left in the current selection; a peer whose addresses
      changed keeps its reservation and receives the new addresses.

crates:
  - name: cumulus-client-collator-discovery
    bump: patch
